.TH LIBEVMAN 3 2026-10-19 "Peios peiosutils 0.8.18"
.SH NAME
libevman \- event catalog parsing and lookup library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <peios/evman.h>

.B "uint32_t peios_evman_abi_version(void);"
.B "peios_evman_catalog *peios_evman_load(peios_evman_bytes directory);"
.B "peios_evman_catalog *peios_evman_parse(const peios_evman_source *, size_t count);"
.B "peios_evman_matches *peios_evman_query(const peios_evman_catalog *, uint32_t mode, peios_evman_bytes text);"
.B "void peios_evman_catalog_free(peios_evman_catalog *);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_catalog_error(const peios_evman_catalog *);"
.B "peios_evman_bytes peios_evman_catalog_message(const peios_evman_catalog *);"
.B "void peios_evman_matches_free(peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_matches_error(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "peios_evman_bytes peios_evman_matches_message(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "size_t peios_evman_finding_count(const peios_evman_catalog *);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_finding(const peios_evman_catalog *, size_t index, peios_evman_finding_view *);"
.B "size_t peios_evman_record_count(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "uint32_t peios_evman_match_kind(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_record(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t index, peios_evman_record_view *);"
.B "peios_evman_bytes peios_evman_qualifier(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "peios_evman_bytes peios_evman_attribute(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "peios_evman_bytes peios_evman_prefix(const peios_evman_matches *);"
.B "size_t peios_evman_header_count(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_header(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record, size_t index, peios_evman_header_view *);"
.B "size_t peios_evman_include_count(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_include(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record, size_t index, peios_evman_line_view *);"
.B "size_t peios_evman_line_count(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record);"
.B "int32_t peios_evman_line(const peios_evman_matches *, size_t record, size_t index, peios_evman_line_view *);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libevman
loads or parses event catalog sources, validates them together, and queries
the resulting catalog.
Source paths identify providers; source text is UTF-8.
Filesystem paths retain their raw Unix bytes.
.PP
Format and cross-source validation findings accompany a usable catalog.
They are separate from operation errors.
A finding reports its source, one-based line, rule number, and message;
rule zero denotes a format issue.
.PP
Query modes are PEIOS_EVMAN_LOOKUP, PEIOS_EVMAN_SEARCH, and PEIOS_EVMAN_ALL.
Search splits text on whitespace.
Each query result owns copies of its records and can outlive its catalog.
Record getters expose event, field, or group identity, source, provider,
body, headers, included groups, and field lines.
Match metadata distinguishes event, field, variant, attribute, index,
search, and all-entry results.
.PP
Record kinds use FIELD=1, GROUP=2, and EVENT=3.
Field-line kinds use FIELD=1 and INCLUDE=2.
The group-include getter returns absent presence, values, and closed fields.
Event field and include lines have present, possibly empty, presence text
and optional values and closed text.
Event lines also expose their indented Markdown explanation as gloss text,
with surrounding blank lines removed; an empty explanation is present and empty.
Group includes have an absent gloss.
An absent optional field differs from a present empty field.
Indexed getters return a POSIX code and leave output untouched on failure.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Operations return an owned handle on success and on failure.
Check the matching error accessor before reading results; zero means success
and a nonzero value is a POSIX error number, independent of errno.
A diagnostic message is borrowed from a failed handle.
A null handle has error EINVAL and no message.
.PP
Free every handle exactly once with its matching free function, including
handles describing failed operations.
Freeing null is harmless.
Returned byte spans and record views remain valid only while their owning
handle remains alive.
Counts return zero for failed or null handles; check the error first.
.PP
Input byte spans are borrowed for the duration of the call.
A null pointer with zero length denotes absence; a non-null zero-length span
is an explicitly empty value.
Lengths exceeding the addressable Rust slice range and null pointers with
nonzero lengths are rejected.
Other non-null pointers must identify valid, readable allocations.
Output pointers and arrays must have the alignment required by their C type.
Text spans contain UTF-8 without a required terminating null byte.
.PP
Read-only access can occur concurrently.
Destruction requires exclusive ownership and ends all borrowed views.
Allocation exhaustion follows the Rust allocator's process-abort policy;
it is not reported as a recoverable ENOMEM result.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid spans, invalid UTF-8 text, an unknown query mode, a null required
handle or output pointer, or an invalid source array.
.TP
.B ERANGE
An indexed getter requested an entry outside the available range.
.TP
.B ENOENT
A lookup did not find the requested event, field, or other catalog entry.
.TP
.B EIO
Reading the catalog directory failed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EVMAN_DIR
Catalog directory used when no explicit directory is supplied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/evman
Default event catalog directory.
.SH NOTES
The runtime SONAME is libevman.so.1 and the ABI version function returns 1.
Use the evman pkg-config module for compiler and linker options.
The Rust wrapper is the peios-evman crate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR evman (1),
